# Hackathon Project Rules

## Core Architecture & Stack
- Stack: Vite + React + Tailwind CSS
- Animation: GSAP (with ScrollTrigger) + Lenis (@studio-freight/react-lenis)
- Motion & Icons: Framer Motion + Lucide Icons (lucide-react)
- Logic Layer: Zustand (zustand), Zod (zod), Radash (radash)
- Logic File: Keep core algorithms inside src/utils/logicEngine.js
- Store File: Maintain client-side global state and seed data in src/store/useStore.js

## Performance Guidelines
- GPU Acceleration: ONLY animate `transform` and `opacity`.
- React Lifecycle: Always wrap GSAP timelines inside `gsap.context()` inside `useLayoutEffect` to clean up on unmount.
- Smooth Scroll Sync: Synchronize GSAP `ScrollTrigger.update()` with the Lenis RAF loop.

# Official Hackathon Judging Criteria (100 Points Total)
1. Functionality & Execution (25 pts):
   - Zero runtime errors or broken UI states.
   - Always pre-load realistic mock demo data in Zustand so features work out of the box upon page load.

2. Innovation & Originality (20 pts):
   - Highlight unique problem-solving features, dynamic workflows, and interactive tooltips/modals.

3. Technical Implementation (20 pts):
   - Keep business logic and data transformations strictly in `src/utils/logicEngine.js`.
   - Maintain client-side global state and seed data in `src/store/useStore.js`.
   - Use Zod schemas to validate inputs and data structures.

4. UI/UX & Usability (15 pts):
   - Deliver a modern dark-mode aesthetic using Tailwind CSS.
   - Include crisp visual icons (`lucide-react`), smooth transitions (`framer-motion`), GSAP scroll effects, and Lenis smooth scrolling.

5. Problem Relevance (10 pts):
   - Strictly solve the target problem statement without unnecessary bloat.

6. Presentation & Deliverables (10 pts):
   - Clean README.md explaining architecture, setup, tools used, and AI disclosure.
